WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.800
What were the events and traumas that shaped
Hannibal Lecter into the weirdly beloved serial

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:05.560
killer he became?

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:09.820
The fava beans are stewing and the Chianti
is decanting we're having lots of old friends

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.240
for dinner to explore Hannibal Lecter's story.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:18.660
Hannibal Lecter was born on January 20, 1933
in the southeastern region of Lithuania to

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.960
a family of great wealth and noble bloodline.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:25.320
His Lithuanian father, Count Lecter, was a
direct descendent of warlord Hannibal the

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:29.420
Grim, while his Italian mother's ancestors
ruled Milan for over two centuries.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:30.900
"They lived like they had money."

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:35.660
Hannibal's education began early, and his
teachers quickly discovered his extraordinary

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.300
intellect, along with a gift for learning
languages.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:42.040
By the time he was 10 years old, Hannibal
could speak Lithuanian, German, English, and

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.920
Italian, and he was on the road to being fluent
in Latin.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:47.480
In 1939 his sister Mischa was born.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:51.240
Hannibal was extremely protective of her and
cared for her more than anyone.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.760
It wasn't long after her birth, however, that
tragedy befell the Lecter family.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:59.000
In 1941, they were forced to flee their castle
when Nazi troops invaded.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:03.870
A small group of Nazis, lead by a brutish
sadist named Vladis Grutas, found the Lecters

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:06.040
and killed the parents in front of Hannibal
and Mischa.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.520
The children were kidnapped and held prisoner
until food ran out.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:13.880
It was then that Grutas cooked Mischa in a
stew in front of Hannibal and forced him to

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:14.380
eat it.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:17.500
Still in shackles, eight-year-old Hannibal
escaped into the woods.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:23.000
By the grace of wartime alliances, young Hannibal
was found wandering in the woods by Soviet

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:23.500
soldiers.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:27.380
The trauma he'd survived turned him mute,
although he'd fully repressed the memory of

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:28.580
what happened with his sister.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:32.720
By this time, the Russians occupied Castle
Lecter and turned it into an orphanage for

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:33.940
children like Hannibal.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:36.340
"It's not healing to see your childhood home.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:42.780
But it helps you measure whether you are broken,
how and why, assuming you want to know."

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:47.500
His fellow orphans considered Hannibal's muteness
a sign of weakness, and he was bullied mercilessly

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:48.000
for it.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:52.280
Hannibal took the abuse, but when he saw other
younger children being bullied, he began to

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.540
lash out violently.

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:57.500
Hannibal Lecter's particular code for choosing
his victims began here.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:01.560
But, though he was involved in many physical
altercations, he had yet to kill.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:06.940
After Hannibal's 13th birthday, his uncle,
Count Robert Lecter, arrived at the castle

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:08.720
turned orphanage to adopt his nephew.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:12.680
Hannibal went to live with Uncle Robert and
his wife, Lady Murasakiin their country home

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:13.380
in France.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:17.500
Hannibal was still mute, but he and Lady Murasaki
had an instant connection.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:22.020
Using martial arts, cooking, and meditation,
she helped Hannibal begin to heal, and he

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.940
developed a taste for the finer things in
life.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:28.660
When he started to speak again, Hannibal added
Japanese to his list of fluent languages.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.340
But tragedy would befall young Hannibal once
more.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.740
When a local butcher hurled insults at Lady
Murasaki, Hannibal attacked the man.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.959
Later, when his Uncle Robert heard about the
altercation, he confronted the butcher and,

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:42.300
in the resulting fray, had a heart attack
and died.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:47.219
In a haze of rage and grief, Lecter stalked
and killed the butcher using one of Lady Murasaki's

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:48.260
samurai swords.

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:52.480
He cut out the man's cheeks and ate them,
marking both his first kill, and his first

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.240
act of cannibalism by choice.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:59.040
"I would have used the butcher's knife, but
the sword seems so appropriate."

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:03.000
Local law enforcement knew that Hannibal had
killed the butcher, but since he passed a

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:06.620
lie detector test with a convincing story,
they were forced to let him go.

00:03:07.799 --> 00:03:11.790
In the wake of Robert Lecter's tragic and
untimely death, Hannibal and Lady Murasaki

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:12.800
moved to Paris.

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:17.280
Hannibal's exceptional intelligence landed
him a spot in a highly esteemed boarding school,

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.500
where he focused on medicine.

00:03:18.909 --> 00:03:23.060
He completed his diploma in record time, graduating
with honors as the youngest person in the

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:23.920
school's history.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:28.180
At 18, Hannibal returned to the cabin in Lithuania
where his family was murdered.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:32.700
After he gave his sister's bones a proper
burial, Hannibal found the dog tags belonging

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:35.020
to the brutes who killed her, and something
snapped.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:39.460
He went after each of the men with cold precision,
removing their cheeks to eat them.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:43.640
Hannibal was now on police radar, and they
were convinced he was a serial killer.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.980
"He was killed in the woods where your family
died.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.680
His face had been eaten."

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:52.420
In retaliation for the killings, Vladis Grutas
kidnapped Lady Murasaki, and she was nearly

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:52.920
killed.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:57.280
When Grutas reminded Hannibal of his own part
in his sister's cannibalism, the repressed

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:00.180
memory pushed Hannibal from methodical to
crazed killer.

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:05.080
This monster frightened Lady Murasaki so deeply
that she fled France and went into hiding.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.700
Hannibal never sought her out again.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:12.159
While Hannibal was in jail awaiting trial
for Grutas' killing, he began to do work sketching

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:14.560
post-autopsy bodies for the medical examiner.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:18.860
When public outcry led to a full acquittal,
Hannibal took an internship at Johns Hopkins

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:22.220
in Baltimore, which turned into university
and postgraduate studies.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:27.020
"Well, now I understand why your drawings
earned you an internship at Johns Hopkins."

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:31.720
Hannibal became a highly regarded psychiatrist
with a reputation for throwing exquisite dinner

00:04:31.729 --> 00:04:36.240
parties, during which he would often feed
choice morsels of his victims to his unsuspecting

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:37.020
guests.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:41.660
One of his patients, the millionaire Mason
Verger, was a sadistic sexual assailant who

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:45.400
had attacked his younger sister so badly,
she would never be able to have children.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:49.900
When he discovered Mason's crime, Hannibal
drugged him with hallucinogens and suggested

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:51.480
Mason cut up his own face.

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:55.800
He did, and came out of the ordeal as a paraplegic
with a lifelong grudge.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:05:00.260
Around this time, Hannibal began to consult
with Detective Will Graham on a serial killer

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:02.180
case, which he happened to be behind.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:06.200
When Will discovered Hannibal's true identity,
they nearly killed each other in a violent

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:06.700
showdown.

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:12.540
In 2013, showrunner Bryan Fuller created an
arthouse version of Hannibal Lecter's story

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:16.800
that drew heavily from previous books and
movies while it simultaneously created a new

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:17.300
narrative.

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:22.000
Fuller's Hannibal was in his 40s, with a backstory
that saw him go to Florence as a young man

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.380
and start his killing there.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:27.960
Inspired by The Monster of Florence serial
killer, Fuller drew from the real-life set

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:32.260
of 16 ritualized killings that took place
between 1968 and1985.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:36.360
"I met him, 20 years ago.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.660
Il Mostro, the Monster of Florence."

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.740
Fuller's Hannibal was also the Baltimore PD's
on-call psychiatrist for profiling purposes.

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:49.120
He didn't just work sporadically with the
department.

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:53.479
He acted as therapist to many of his colleagues,
including Will Graham, with whom he had a

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:55.920
deeply intense and complicated relationship.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:58.840
This version of Hannibal wasn't just the Chesapeake
Ripper.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:02.820
He often mimicked the killings of those he'd
been tasked to help catch, adding to their

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:03.820
body counts.

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:08.909
"Is the organ harvester disguising his work
as the crimes of a serial killer, or is a

00:06:08.909 --> 00:06:12.080
serial killer disguising his crimes as the
work of an organ harvester?"

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:17.300
The show's three-season run offered a textbook
manual on how to identify Hannibal's gaslighting

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:21.380
practices, which he used to frame Graham for
a series of killings he himself committed,

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:24.660
all the while convincing Graham that he actually
was responsible.

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:29.780
Bryan Fuller's Hannibal didn't just deepen
the relationship between Will and Hannibal.

00:06:29.789 --> 00:06:33.620
A number of key characters were added, who
helped make this new iteration of Hannibal

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:35.120
Lecter profoundly three-dimensional.

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:39.540
Many of them appeared marginally in Thomas
Harris' books, but Fuller gave them new life.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:44.300
In this version, Lady Murasaki's maid Chiyoh
helped Hannibal find, torture, and imprison

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:45.540
the men who killed his sister.

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:51.080
A gender-flipped Dr. Alana Bloom, first mentioned
in Red Dragon as Alan, became a pivotal figure

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:55.689
torn between helping a troubled Will Graham
and actively being gaslighted by her serial

00:06:55.689 --> 00:06:56.780
killer boyfriend, Hannibal.

00:06:57.240 --> 00:07:01.000
Red Dragon's relentless tabloid journalist
Freddie Lounds was also gender-flipped.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:06.670
New characters included FBI Agent Miriam Lass,
who discovered Hannibal's identity but disappeared

00:07:06.670 --> 00:07:07.980
before she could tell anyone.

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:12.220
Lass was presumed dead when her severed arm
was identified, but it was later discovered

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:15.320
that Hannibal had kept her alive for years
in an underground bunker.

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:20.000
And Fuller's Hannibal introduced the killer's
own therapist, Bedelia Du Maurier, who provided

00:07:20.009 --> 00:07:24.720
incredible insight into Hannibal's mind, as
well as a sense of fear about who, or what,

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:25.960
she suspected him to be.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:29.040
"What Hannibal does is not coercion.

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:32.700
It is persuasion."

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:37.800
Hannibal Lecter was convicted of multiple
homicides and remanded to Baltimore State

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:39.680
Hospital for the Criminally Insane.

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:44.120
Hospital staff soon learned Hannibal was unlike
any of the other psychopaths housed in their

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:44.620
facility.

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:49.740
He was a master of self-control, able to manipulate
his body and vital functions with such precision

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:51.180
as to fool machines.

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:55.789
He actively cultivated his so-called "Memory
Palace," detailed rooms in his mind filled

00:07:55.789 --> 00:07:58.640
with art, books, and places he hoped to see
again in person.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:02.400
"My palace is vast, even by medieval standards."

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:07.140
One day, Hannibal faked a seizure and proceeded
to kill a nurse, just because he could.

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:11.840
The incident forced hospital administrator
Fredrick Chilton to create entirely new protocols

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:15.860
on how to handle Hannibal, which included
absolutely no physical contact.

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:20.120
Hannibal's only ally was Barney, a compassionate
orderly who became as friendly with him as

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:20.920
anyone could.

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:24.659
While Hannibal might have been one of the
most disturbing serial killers ever caught,

00:08:24.659 --> 00:08:29.090
he was also still one of the psychiatric community's
greatest minds, especially when it came to

00:08:29.090 --> 00:08:30.160
people like himself.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:35.480
In 1978, Will Graham came out of retirement
to help Baltimore PD with a series of brutal

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:38.000
family murders that were taking place on a
lunar cycle.

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:39.080
"It won't stop."

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:41.740
"Why not?"

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:44.180
"Cause it makes him God.

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:46.680
Would you give that up?"

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:51.220
Will approached Hannibal once more for help,
and together they identified the "Tooth Fairy"

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:56.000
killer as Francis Dolarhyde, a film tech who
was choosing targets through their home videos.

00:08:56.230 --> 00:09:00.120
The case ended with Dolarhyde's death, but
Hannibal continued to write Will letters,

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:03.140
claiming that Will was the only person in
the world who truly knew him.

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:07.880
Hannibal Lecter would have no contact with
anyone other than Fredrick Chilton, Barney,

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:09.760
and other orderlies for the next five years.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:14.020
That's when the FBI sent in Special Agent
Clarice Starling to get Hannibal to talk about

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:18.120
a former patient who was suspected of being
a serial killer known as "Buffalo Bill."

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:22.260
Hannibal saw right through Clarice, but he
also found himself drawn to her.

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:25.960
"Now this ham-handed segway into your questionnaire.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.320
It won't do."

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:33.951
In a cruel game of quid pro quo, he got her
to reveal personal details about her life

00:09:33.951 --> 00:09:38.060
in exchange for information about Buffalo
Bill, although only some of what Hannibal

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:39.760
told her turned out to be true.

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:44.600
While Clarice earned her FBI badge, Hannibal
staged an elaborate escape that involved wearing

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.820
the face of a police officer monitoring him.

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:50.620
He wound up in the Bahamas, where Fredrick
Chilton happened to be vacationing.

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:54.220
Hannibal called Clarice to tell her he wouldn't
be seeking her out, and said:

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:56.600
"I have no plans to call on you, Clarice.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:59.120
The world's more interesting with you in it."

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:02.100
He then implied he'd be seeing Chilton soon, and said:

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:04.620
"I'm having an old friend for dinner."

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:07.520
Chilton was never seen or heard from again.

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:12.720
Following his escape, Hannibal Lecter went
through extensive plastic surgery on his face,

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:16.480
sparing only his nose for fear he'd lose his
extra-sensitive sense of smell.

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:21.000
He started going by Dr. Fell and set up shop
in Florence, where he rebranded himself as

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.960
an art expert and museum curator.

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:26.880
"They are letting me look after the library,
for a stipend."

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:31.240
Hannibal was of Italian heritage on his mother's
side, so he began to investigate his bloodline

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:33.080
alongside his curatorial duties.

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:36.520
But despite his efforts, he wasn't as incognito
as he thought.

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:40.760
Mason Verger had been stewing in his rage
for years, and he'd put a multi-million dollar

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:42.820
price tag on Hannibal's whereabouts.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:47.260
He planned to enact his revenge by feeding
his old nemesis alive to wild boars.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:51.860
In the meantime, a disgraced Clarice Starling,
who had been demoted following a botched heist,

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:55.820
figured out what Mason Verger had planned
and attempted to find Lecter first in an effort

00:10:55.820 --> 00:10:56.860
to save her career.

00:10:57.400 --> 00:11:01.720
Hannibal kidnapped Clarice, and Mason's younger
sister killed her brother, a crime that Hannibal

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:02.620
took the fall for.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:07.660
Hannibal slowly came to accept how the horrific
trauma of being forced to eat his own sister

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:09.980
had shaped his subsequent crimes and desires.

00:11:10.280 --> 00:11:13.360
While he was attracted to Clarice, he also
saw his sister in her.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:16.840
"Will you stay with me in my prison cell and
hold my hand, Clarice?

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:18.820
We could have some fun."

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:23.760
Her anecdotes from their quid pro quo game
all those years ago created a soft spot in

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:25.640
Hannibal, leaving him oddly protective of
her.

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:28.600
"And he was fond of her?"

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:32.040
"Yes."

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:35.280
Even so, this didn't stop Hannibal from hurting
Clarice.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:39.640
He attempted to brainwash her into believing
she really was Mischa in order to have a proxy

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:44.600
of his sister back, but Clarice was too strong
mentally, and she overpowered Hannibal's attempts.

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:49.280
During that process of hypnosis, though, Clarice
was altered mentally, and she became a different

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:51.780
kind of student of Hannibal's singular psychopathy.

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:55.620
The two became romantically involved and were
last spotted in Buenos Aires.

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:59.990
It remains unclear whether Clarice was with
him because of his hold over her, or if she'd

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:03.320
actually chosen to align herself with the
serial killer she once hunted.

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:05.980
"Would you ever say to me, stop?

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:09.120
If you loved me you'd stop."

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:12.540
"Not in a thousand years."

